Subject: DXVK d3d9: request geometry shaders and cull distance only if offered
Date: 2026-10-24
Applies to: sources/dxvk (DXVK 1.10.3 cxaddon) from crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
Files changed: src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp, src/d3d9/d3d9_include.h

CrossOver's DXVK requires geometryShader and shaderCullDistance for Direct3D
9. CodeWeavers' MoltenVK 1.2.10 has geometry shaders but no cull distance
(the menu stayed black), Khronos' MoltenVK 1.4.2 has cull distance but no
geometry shaders (vkCreateDevice fails with VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT for
features 5 and 39). Direct3D 9 shaders only write clip distances, and
geometry shaders serve some meta operations, so both are requested only when
the device offers them.

d3d9_include.h: current MinGW headers define D3DDEVINFO_RESOURCEMANAGER;
DXVK's own definition is removed. Build with -Dcpp_args='-include cstdint'
for GCC 16 (see build/build.sh).

Test on MoltenVK 1.4.2 (tests/src/d3d9-*-test): device created;
shader, format, VPOS and texture matrix tests correct; the clear test is
wrong (draws after a clear inside a frame are missing).
Review fixes (2026-10-24):
- SupportsSWVP() also requires geometryShader: software vertex processing
  (ProcessVertices) writes its output from a geometry shader. On MoltenVK
  1.4.2 it used to run without one and write zeros; now it is refused, as on
  devices without vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics.
Test: tests/src/d3d9-swvp-test.c.
License: zlib, like the DXVK files it modifies.
---
diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
index 23b0a6f..2099a55 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp
@@ -2613,7 +2613,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
       static bool s_errorShown = false;
 
       if (!std::exchange(s_errorShown, true))
-        Logger::err("D3D9DeviceEx::ProcessVertices: SWVP emu unsupported (vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics)");
+        Logger::err("D3D9DeviceEx::ProcessVertices: SWVP emu unsupported (vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics, geometryShader)");
 
       return D3D_OK;
     }
@@ -3901,7 +3901,10 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
 
   bool D3D9DeviceEx::SupportsSWVP() {
-    return m_dxvkDevice->features().core.features.vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics;
+    // The emulation writes vertices from a geometry shader, which some
+    // devices lack (MoltenVK 1.4.2): refuse there instead of writing garbage.
+    const auto& features = m_dxvkDevice->features().core.features;
+    return features.vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics && features.geometryShader;
   }
 
 
@@ -3914,8 +3917,9 @@ namespace dxvk {
     DxvkDeviceFeatures supported = adapter->features();
     DxvkDeviceFeatures enabled = {};
 
-    // Geometry shaders are used for some meta ops
-    enabled.core.features.geometryShader = VK_TRUE;
+    // Geometry shaders are used for some meta ops. MoltenVK 1.4.2 has none;
+    // request them only when the device offers them.
+    enabled.core.features.geometryShader = supported.core.features.geometryShader;
     enabled.core.features.robustBufferAccess = VK_TRUE;
     enabled.extRobustness2.robustBufferAccess2 = supported.extRobustness2.robustBufferAccess2;
 
@@ -3944,7 +3948,9 @@ namespace dxvk {
     enabled.core.features.sampleRateShading = VK_TRUE;
     enabled.core.features.samplerAnisotropy = supported.core.features.samplerAnisotropy;
     enabled.core.features.shaderClipDistance = VK_TRUE;
-    enabled.core.features.shaderCullDistance = VK_TRUE;
+    // D3D9 shaders only write clip distances; CodeWeavers' MoltenVK 1.2.10
+    // has no cull distance support.
+    enabled.core.features.shaderCullDistance = supported.core.features.shaderCullDistance;
 
     // Ensure we support real BC formats and unofficial vendor ones.
     enabled.core.features.textureCompressionBC = VK_TRUE;
diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_include.h b/src/d3d9/d3d9_include.h
index 8762265..adb1ad3 100644
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_include.h
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_include.h
@@ -79,10 +79,7 @@
 
 // MinGW headers are broken. Who'dve guessed?
 #ifndef _MSC_VER
-typedef struct _D3DDEVINFO_RESOURCEMANAGER
-{
-  char dummy;
-} D3DDEVINFO_RESOURCEMANAGER, * LPD3DDEVINFO_RESOURCEMANAGER;
+/* D3DDEVINFO_RESOURCEMANAGER: defined by current MinGW headers. */
 
 #ifndef __WINE__
 extern "C" WINUSERAPI WINBOOL WINAPI SetProcessDPIAware(VOID);
